1. THE EIGHT POLYGONS WITH phi(n) = 36 = 2^2 3^2
   (Z/n)* = Gal(Q(zeta_n)/Q), order 36;  G+ = (Z/n)*/{+-1} = Gal(Q(cos 2pi/n)/Q), order 18.
     n    lattice parts of (2,2)        (Z/n)*              G+ (real field)     trisections   the two cubic steps
     37   37:(2,2)                      C4 x C9             C2 x C9                  2        nested (cyclic C9)
     57   3^1:(1,0) + 19:(1,2)          C2 x C2 x C9        C2 x C9                  2        nested (cyclic C9)
     63   3^2:(1,1) + 7:(1,1)           C2 x C2 x C3 x C3   C2 x C3 x C3             2        independent (C3 x C3)
     74   37:(2,2)                      C4 x C9             C2 x C9                  2        nested (cyclic C9)
     76   2^2:(1,0) + 19:(1,2)          C2 x C2 x C9        C2 x C9                  2        nested (cyclic C9)
    108   2^2:(1,0) + 3^3:(1,2)         C2 x C2 x C9        C2 x C9                  2        nested (cyclic C9)
    114   3^1:(1,0) + 19:(1,2)          C2 x C2 x C9        C2 x C9                  2        nested (cyclic C9)
    126   3^2:(1,1) + 7:(1,1)           C2 x C2 x C3 x C3   C2 x C3 x C3             2        independent (C3 x C3)
   group types of order 36: C4xC9, C2xC2xC9, C4xC3xC3, C2xC2xC3xC3;  realised: all but C4 x C3 x C3.

